tive Resource Wrappers</h3>\n<p><strong>Overall Score:</strong> 0.65</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>The image processing library utilizes native code (JNI) or java.awt components that rely on the Finalizer mechanism. If objects holding native memory handles are created at high frequency, they populate the Finalizer queue. If the Finalizer thread is lagging or blocked, the heap fills with 'zombie' objects. ImageProcessor threads are WAITING because they are synchronized on a lock needed by the Finalizer thread or waiting for exhausted native resources.</p>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Metrics:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Explanatory Power: 0.90</li>\n<li>Simplicity: 0.50</li>\n<li>Testability: 0.80</li>\n<li>Prior Probability: 0.40</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supporting Evidence:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Observation 2 (GC doesn't reclaim space) is a hallmark of finalization lag.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Contradicting Evidence:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Modern JVMs (Java 11+) have moved away from Finalizers toward Cleaners, which are less prone to this specific type of total stall.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Testable Predictions:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Running jmap -finalizerinfo <pid> will show a massive and growing number of objects waiting for finalization.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Status:</strong> ✅ Hypotheses generated and evaluated</p>\n\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"tab-content\" data-tab=\"Markdown\">\n<pre><code class=\"language-markdown\">\n## Generated Hypotheses\n\n**Count:** 3\n\n---\n\n### Hypothesis 1: Unbounded Work Queue with Consumer Starvation\n\n**Overall Score:** 0.93\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe 'Image Processing' module uses an unbounded task queue (like LinkedBlockingQueue) where an upstream producer adds images faster than the ImageProcessor threads—which are currently blocked—can process them. Memory increases as image data is pushed into the queue indefinitely. GC cannot reclaim these reachable objects. ImageProcessor threads are in a WAITING st