ed at high frequency, they populate the Finalizer queue. If the Finalizer thread is lagging or blocked, the heap fills with 'zombie' objects. ImageProcessor threads are WAITING because they are synchronized on a lock needed by the Finalizer thread or waiting for exhausted native resources.\n\n**Evaluation Metrics:**\n- Explanatory Power: 0.90\n- Simplicity: 0.50\n- Testability: 0.80\n- Prior Probability: 0.40\n\n**Supporting Evidence:**\n- Observation 2 (GC doesn't reclaim space) is a hallmark of finalization lag.\n\n**Contradicting Evidence:**\n- Modern JVMs (Java 11+) have moved away from Finalizers toward Cleaners, which are less prone to this specific type of total stall.\n\n**Testable Predictions:**\n- Running jmap -finalizerinfo &lt;pid&gt; will show a massive and growing number of objects waiting for finalization.\n\n---\n\n**Status:** ✅ Hypotheses generated and evaluated\n</code></pre>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"tab-content\" data-tab=\"Hide\">\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"